<article class="env-exercise" id="0CT2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CT2">Exercise <span data-tag="0CT2">111.12.8</span>.</a> Let $(R, \mathfrak m)$ be a Noetherian local ring. Let $x, y \in \mathfrak m$ be a regular sequence of length $2$. For any $n \geq 2$ show that there do not exist $a, b \in R$ with </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  x^{n - 1}y^{n - 1} = a x^ n + b y^ n  \]
</div>
  <p> Suggestion: First try for $n = 2$ to see how to argue. Remark: There is a vast generalization of this result called the monomial conjecture. </p>
</article>